From: Guanyi Chen <felixlinker02@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] amdgpu: accept VRAM buffers in dma_buf_map

After pinning buffers to VRAM (patch 2/3), the buffer's mem_type
becomes TTM_PL_VRAM. The original map function only accepts
TTM_PL_TT and returns -EBUSY for anything else, which rejects
VRAM-pinned buffers.

Extend the condition to accept both TTM_PL_TT and TTM_PL_VRAM.
When mem_type is TTM_PL_VRAM, the existing code path calls
amdgpu_vram_mgr_alloc_sgt() which generates an sg_table with DMA
addresses based on the GPU BAR physical address.

Signed-off-by: Guanyi Chen <felixlinker02@gmail.com>
---
 amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
@@ -316,7 +316,7 @@
 		if (r)
 			return ERR_PTR(r);
 
-	} else if (bo->tbo.resource->mem_type != TTM_PL_TT) {
+	} else if (bo->tbo.resource->mem_type != TTM_PL_TT && bo->tbo.resource->mem_type != TTM_PL_VRAM) {
 		return ERR_PTR(-EBUSY);
 	}
 #else
